body:
Addendum to next-all-host-restart-checklist-2026-11-13 (Termal::Fable2, 2026-11-13 23:27Z). Remove it after the restart is verified.

1. Engram w-baa6 cutover (sync A→B→A, R12 31c17d19)
- Engram::Fable proposed the plan in ebe242f7 #7862; TermAl concurred in #7863 under 4 conditions.
- The hazard: its new CompletionReported event can't be decoded by OLD engram processes sharing the store.
- The plan:
  - The Merger lands it once gated.
  - It installs on Central and DL560 ONLY right before the held joint RESET NOW.
  - It runs readiness on all stores, then sends "installed + ready".
  - I send the RESET NOW within minutes, with one added line naming the Engram build sha256 + fingerprint per host.
  - After the restart, the Merger confirms that no pre-install engram process remains.
  - If the restart slips, the binary waits uninstalled.
- My conditions:
  - No task-sync import on any host from the install until that confirmation; Engram confirms whether ordinary words can emit CompletionReported.
  - Explain how the old Mac build is kept from receiving CompletionReported via sync.
  - A backup before each swap.
  - The RESET NOW line above.

2. 657d (w-657d74d6944b)
- Greg said YES to the HandingOff rewording („mozemy wzonowic…”, 588693a8 #1595).
- Recorded on the item with my concurrence. edfd applies holder note bca80c6d via revise.

3. Owner for the 11th C5 Medium
- w-54e15402ea0e goes to edfd, after its 3186 fix 7fc4a0dc.

23:28Z, Engram::Fable #7864: all 4 conditions ACCEPTED.
(1) Verified in 31c17d19: the only writer of CompletionReported is task_sync::reported::apply_on (reported.rs:138), called only from folder_admission.rs:854 (the task-sync folder import). Ordinary work words never emit it. Order stands.
(2) The event is created only in the importing host's local store; the exchange carries task text, not events. Still, no old-build host takes part in task-sync exchange until it carries the new build, and the Mac's Engram stays out of sync until then. 12325 will confirm that the exported document format is unchanged.
(3) Create-only dated backups under ~/.engram/backups on both hosts, with paths and hashes recorded.
(4) The sha256 and build_fingerprint per host come with "installed + ready".

01:44Z Nov 14, Engram::Fable #7867: baa6 candidate 31c17d19 will NOT land. 12325 is fixing an in-scope order-dependent fixture (corrections.rs:626, "prerequisites must be sorted and unique"), so the install at the held restart moves to the NEW candidate; its sha256 and fingerprint come later, at "installed + ready". The Engram Windows trio (w-ab27, w-a76f, w-728a) lands first as bf8ce052 on 75af1b27, after combo99c. The Merger's stall warnings are Engram's own code, filed as Engram w-710ef837c24b (P2). The 4 cutover conditions are unchanged.

04:14Z Nov 14: NEXT RESET NOW agreed with Engram::Fable (#7874/#7875). Send it through Asistant right after Opus3's verified push of master eb78d349 → 772f1da1 (scroll + board; FULL test-bd497993 on Central started ~04:13Z, ends ~05:15-05:25Z), so about 05:30Z. No Engram install rides along; Central and DL560 keep w-180d, which the restart finally loads into every engram MCP. Nothing may straddle; an Engram job running at send time is just marked INTERRUPTED. Greg's procedure is unchanged (stop, paired dated backup of termal.sqlite* and coordination.sqlite*, git pull, cargo run --release); Central and DL560 move together; the Mac is best-effort. After „zaczynam”:
- Engram::Fable takes one wake at +15 min;
- the Merger re-sights w-3b's root (the f5dc fix);
- Opus2 attests the running builds;
- I send the "hosts back" notice;
- evaluations go via Opus2's GO;
- criterion-6 evidence follows per Opus3's checklist, including agy;
- the no-rerun memory can then be removed (d922 is live).

04:37Z Nov 14: the scroll+board FULL test-bd497993 (772f1da1) FAILED. scripts/test-launcher.test.mjs:314 hit the known w-e879 stderr-warning defect under Central load; ui/ is not the cause, and it was preserved, not rerun. Greg's direction (Asistant #1623) = option A: a combined candidate of e879 8e54644b plus the 20 ui/ paths of 772f1da1, one cold Central FULL after the e879 WHOLE4 pair is clean (~05:00Z), ending ~06:20Z. The PUSH needs Greg's OWN word for the combined change in Opus3's session (CLAUDE.md: relayed words never carry a push), and Opus3 pushes after Opus2's GO. The RESET NOW is held until that push is verified, ~06:30Z; it then also loads e879.

04:43Z: the e879 WHOLE4 pair found M1, a Rust transport truncating stderr at 64 KiB (bounded_read_process.rs:309/566), so 8e54644b and combo dca6f762 are BLOCKED and not run. Chosen A2 (Opus2 #6067, Fable2 #3151/#6068):
- 03d4 cuts a LAUNCHER-ONLY e879 slice (scripts/test-launcher-input.mjs and its test) on eb78d349;
- quick Node check on DL560, then a small fresh pair;
- then a combo of slice + byte-identical scroll+board, cold FULL on Central ~05:10-06:15Z;
- Greg's own word in Opus3's session, Opus3 pushes, RESET NOW ~06:30Z.
The Rust M1 fix is a second e879 slice later; w-e879 stays open until both land. Greg was told (Asistant #1626).

06:05Z Nov 14: the A2 FULL test-590a0d31 PASSED (05:02:29-06:02:47Z). Opus3 pushed 491dd015, verified by ls-remote at 06:04Z, and main is clean. RESET NOW SENT to Greg via Asistant (#1639), master 491dd015, no Engram install. Engram::Fable and Opus2 are informed. NEXT after „zaczynam”:
- Opus2's per-host attestation;
- Fable2 announces "hosts back" to all coders;
- the Merger re-sights w-3b;
- the GO-EVAL sequence;
- C6 evidence (Opus3 checklist, agy one prompt);
- remove memory no-rerun-on-earned-no-credit-text-2026-11-13 (d922 live);
- the held queue: combo100 (610b+6ea4+96c9), e879 Rust 3f076cc6, 3757B, 4093 R6, 2ecb GREEN, 3186 Windows, w-a57f plan (d50d).
